Project README — Development quickstart

Prerequisites

- Docker (https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/)
- Docker Compose (included in modern Docker; documentation: https://docs.docker.com/compose/)

Before you start

- Verify Docker is installed and running on your machine.
- Review `docker-compose.yml` and `apache/000-default.conf` to adjust any environment-specific settings (ports, mounts, credentials).

Start the development environment

1. Open a terminal in the project root (where `docker-compose.yml` is located).
2. Run:

```bash
docker compose up
```

Add `-d` to run in detached mode:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Stop and remove containers:

```bash
docker compose down
```

If you want, I can expand this README with troubleshooting tips, environment variables, or a short architecture diagram.
